 "equipment_type": "Air handling unit controller",
 "applies_to": "Komfovent air handling units fitted with the C8 controller.",
 "summary": "The Komfovent C8 controller exposes its settings and readings over BACnet IP on its RJ-45 Ethernet port (no MS/TP). The list has 136 objects: temperatures and setpoints as AVs, on/off, enables and alarms as BVs, modes and settings as multistate values, and flows, timers, readings and run-hour counters as positive integer values. Two date values hold the holiday period, and a time value gives the next scheduled mode change.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": 60,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "The two Date Value objects (HOLIDAYS: from / till, instances 0-1) are listed with type Other. The doc also has a Time Value object 0, SCHEDULER: next mode start time (read-only, 00:00-24:00), left out here because it would clash with Other 0.",
  "Mode-specific setpoints, flows and heating flags exist for each mode (away, normal, intensive, boost, kitchen, fireplace, override, holidays).",
  "Mode flows and the current flow readings are in % (20-100 %), not m3/h; the C8 list has no pressure readings or flow-unit setting.",
  "Unlike the C6, the C8 list has no general INFO: alarm BV; use the active alarm count or the ALARMS BVs.",
  "The C8 list adds fire damper alarms and fan / heater / heat exchanger run-hour counters."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "BACnet Connection C8 - Installation and Service Manual",
  "doc_number": "BACnet-C8_26-07",
  "revision_date": "2026-07",
  "url": "https://www.komfovent.com/en/downloads/Bacnet_connection_C8_EN.pdf"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Switch the unit with BV 0 CONTROL: ON/OFF status and select the mode with MV 1 CONTROL: current mode (only away, normal, intensive and boost can be written). Each mode has its own temperature setpoint AV and supply/extract flow PIVs. Read the INFO temperatures and flows, the ALARMS BVs and the active alarm count; writing 39366 to that count resets alarms.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BV 0",
    "name": "CONTROL: ON/OFF status",
    "why": "On/off command (1 = on)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "MV 1",
    "name": "CONTROL: current mode",
    "why": "Mode command; writable values 2-5 (away to boost)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 1",
    "name": "NORMAL: setpoint",
    "why": "Temperature setpoint for NORMAL mode"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 11",
    "name": "INFO: supply temperature",
    "why": "Supply air temperature"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 12",
    "name": "INFO: extract temperature",
    "why": "Extract air temperature"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 13",
    "name": "INFO: outdoor temperature",
    "why": "Outdoor air temperature"
   },
   {
    "ref": "PIV 26",
    "name": "INFO: current supply flow",
    "why": "Supply fan flow, %"
   },
   {
    "ref": "PIV 24",
    "name": "ALARMS: active alarms count",
    "why": "Active alarms (0-10); write 39366 to reset"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "BV 0 CONTROL: ON/OFF status turns the unit on (1) or off (0). BV 2 CONTROL: AUTO mode hands mode selection to the schedule or air quality control (MV 0 shows which).",
  "heartbeat": null,
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "setup": [
   "Factory network settings: DHCP off, IP 192.168.0.60, mask 255.255.255.0, gateway 192.168.0.1, BACnet ID 60.",
   "Change them in the controller web server (Connectivity) or on the control panel (Advanced settings > Connectivity).",
   "Komfovent recommends a polling interval of at least 1 second."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "MV 1 CONTROL: current mode accepts only values 2-5 (away, normal, intensive, boost) as writes.",
   "Writing 39366 to the ALARMS: active alarms count PIV resets alarms.",
   "CONNECTIVITY IP address and mask PIVs are writable; a wrong write can drop the controller off the network.",
   "The RESET SETTINGS multistate value restores factory settings for the chosen group; keep it out of normal BMS writes."
  ]
 },
